message: >-
  If you use this software or these results, please cite the work using the
  metadata below. A persistent repository identifier (DOI) has not yet been
  assigned; the `doi` field will be filled in after archival release.
  `version` 1.0.0 is the intended first-release version; `date-released`
  will be set to the actual release date when the first public release is
  tagged.
title: >-
  Finite-Sample Operating Characteristics and Estimand Characterization of a
  Ratio-Estimation Procedure for Mean-Difference Meta-Analysis
authors:
  - family-names: Sriwicha
    given-names: Phongsakon
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-0561-1076"
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Computer Engineering, Faculty of Engineering,
      King Mongkut's University of Technology Thonburi, Bangkok, Thailand
version: 1.0.0
keywords:
  - meta-analysis
  - mean difference
  - ratio estimation
  - finite-sample inference
  - estimands
  - simulation
  - random effects
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility repository for a simulation study of the finite-sample
  operating characteristics of a published ratio-estimation interval
  procedure for mean-difference meta-analysis, with three prespecified
  variants and three comparator procedures, evaluated on 152 simulation
  cells over three population targets. Contains simulation code, the
  deterministic seed specification, target calculations, archived per-cell
  results, the analysis pipeline, and table/figure generation code.
